From 72ad822990fbe07fe243a5678c8b743290e29c6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 19:42:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/87] iommu: add Verisilicon IOMMU provider and Rockchip
 provider media hooks

The RK3588 vendor media stack needs two things from the IOMMU layer that
mainline does not expose:

  - a provider for the Verisilicon (VSI) IOMMU that sits in front of the AV1
    decoder, added as drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c behind CONFIG_VSI_IOMMU;
  - provider-local control hooks on the existing Rockchip IOMMU
    (enable / disable / force-reset / mask-irq / set-fault-handler) that the
    MPP service uses to disable, re-enable and flush a hardware IOMMU and to
    route pagefaults per hardware core, without relying on BSP-private APIs.

Expose both through include/soc/rockchip/{rockchip_iommu,vsi_iommu}.h so the
media drivers no longer depend on out-of-tree headers, wire up the iommu
Kconfig/Makefile, select VSI_IOMMU from the Hantro Rockchip config, and add
the Verisilicon IOMMU devicetree binding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
